WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.700
Hello everybody, my name is Markiplier, and

00:00:01.700 --> 00:00:07.980
this past weekend, we raised $110,000 dollars for Crisis Text Line.

00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:10.460
That is absolutely astonishing.

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:13.620
Thank you everybody so much for joining the charity livestream

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:17.180
and thank you everybody so much for donating to the cause.

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:19.520
If you don't know about Crisis Text Line, I'll leave a link

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:21.360
in the description below (the links to their website).

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:24.600
You can find out more about them, but I'm sure you know about it

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:27.020
because I blabbered endlessly about it.

00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:28.340
AND it was fun!

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:31.160
It was so much fun to be there with my friends

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:34.880
and the whole gang was able to participate, and you guys were able to play with us.

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:39.100
And it was just a lot of fun, and I know we haven't been doing these charity livestreams

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:45.320
regularly enough, but I guarantee you this is the start of regular monthly charity livestreams.

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:50.140
In fact, Tyler and I are going back home to Cincinnati, and when we are there,

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:56.500
we are hoping to join Bob and Wade in a Cincinnati reunion charity livestream that

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:58.700
should be OODLES of fun.

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:00.400
We just have to set up a few things.

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:03.820
But that will be next month, and we're probably gonna do a Christmas theme to it.

00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:06.980
And also, I wanna do a "12 Days of Christmas" video thing

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:08.440
that we're gonna be doing next month.

00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:12.220
But that's getting a head of myself, because I wanted to talk about this week's videos.

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:16.020
And by the title of this video, which is probably something along the lines of

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:18.060
EMBRACE THE CRINGE!

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:20.340
Um. It was-- It was a lot of fun.

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:22.820
I-I'm not knocking what we did at all.

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:26.380
But it's just that thing about experimenting and trying new things.

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:29.100
And you definitely find the things that don't work!

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:31.000
And I mentioned this on the livestream

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:33.240
We went out to a park and we met with you guys

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:35.020
and it was a great experience, as it always is.

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:39.220
Uhm, but we tried something, which we probably shouldn't have tried

00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:42.520
So-so basically, we out to the park, and it was super awesome

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:45.260
as it always is to meet you guys and be able to do videos with you guys

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:48.960
and there's still another video from that session that's gonna come out later.

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:54.580
But one of the things that we did do was attempt the don't laugh challenge in public.

00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:58.820
And we discovered that, either that doesn't work in general

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:03.880
or we're just not funny, which I'm more inclined to believe the latter

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:05.300
of the two options there.

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:08.820
Because, something about being in public versus

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:11.660
a controlled environment like the office

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:14.440
is just vastly different because

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:18.180
the don't laugh challenge is supposed to be kinda cringey

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:21.940
because there's moments where it doesn't work, they don't laugh!

00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:27.920
And it's just "HEY ok that joke didn't go anywhere gonna step away from the awkwardness now!"

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:30.100
You know, that's part of the experience but

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:32.560
when you're out in a park, you don't get to escape

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:35.240
You don't get to run away when something's bad

00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:38.540
because, the weirdest thing was, there was an audience there!

00:02:38.620 --> 00:02:39.980
You guys were there!

00:02:39.980 --> 00:02:42.640
And you guys don't wanna be mean so

00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:44.840
you kinda half laugh

00:02:45.380 --> 00:02:48.660
but that's so much worse than just dead silence!

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:52.840
Because it's kinda funny, when a joke falls so flat on its face

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:55.840
that it's just crickets is all you can hear

00:02:55.840 --> 00:02:58.820
And sometimes, like that is funny in and of itself

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:00.920
and that's what makes the don't laugh challenge good

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:03.540
but when you get a bad joke and then

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:06.260
"Heh...yeah" *sniffs* "Heheh"

00:03:06.460 --> 00:03:08.480
That is the DEATH of comedy.

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:09.900
That is the death of everything.

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:12.960
And I talked about on the livestream that I was gonna play this and of course I am

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:15.060
Because I'm not gonna shy away from this one

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:19.940
